ation-based planners struggle with contact complexity, while on-policy reinforcement learning (RL) is sample-inefficient and has limited multi-task ability.\nL17: We propose a framework combining a learned world model with sampling-based Model Predictive Control (MPC), trained on a demonstration-free offline dataset to predict future outcomes in a compressed latent space. To address sparse contact rewards and sensor noise, the MPC uses a learned surrogate value function for dense, robust planning.\nL18: Our single, scalable model supports contact-aware tasks, including wall support after perturbation, blocking incoming objects, and traversing height-limited arches, with improved data efficiency and multi-task capability over on-policy RL. Deployed on a physical humanoid, our system achieves robust, real-time contact planning from proprioception and ego-centric depth images. Website: cite16†this https URL†ego-vcp.github.io L19: Subjects:  | Robotics (cs.RO); Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI); Systems and Control (eess.SY)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite17†arXiv:2510.11682 [cs.RO]\nL21:    | (or cite18†arXiv:2510.11682v1 [cs.RO] for this version)\nL22:    | cite19†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2510.11682†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Hang Liu [cite20†view email ]\nL26: [v1] Mon, 13 Oct 2025 17:47:39 UTC (4,374 KB)\nL27: cite5†[v2] Sun, 8 Mar 2026 23:33:03 UTC (4,840 KB)\nL28: \nL29: Full-text links:\nL30: \nL31: ## Access Paper:\nL32: \nL33: View a PDF of the paper titled Ego-Vision World Model for Humanoid Contact Planning, by Hang Liu and 7 other authors\nL34: \nL35:   * cite14†View PDF L36:   * cite15†HTML (experimental) L37:   * cite21†TeX Source L38: \nL39: cite22†view license L40: ### Current browse context:\nL41: \nL42: cs.RO\nL43: \nL44: cite23†< prev |   cite24†next > L45: \nL46: cite25†new | cite26†recent | cite27†2025-10 L47: \nL48: Change to browse by:\nL49: \nL50: c